    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from both directions of the road.\n• Mark the entrance to the detached structure with a reflective address or unit marker so responders can locate it quickly at night or in low visibility.\n• Clear vegetation along the sides of the access drive so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n• Trim dense vegetation near the detached structure to open a clear path for responders approaching on foot.\n• Keep a minimum 10-foot-wide path on the access drive free of parked vehicles, equipment, and debris at all times.\n• Designate and mark a flat, stable area near the access drive where emergency vehicles can turn around.\n• Keep all gates between the main residence and detached structure unlocked or equipped with a lock box accessible to responders.\n• Trim shrubs and low-hanging branches along walkways connecting the main residence to the detached structure.\n• Post a simple site map near the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence, detached structure, and any secondary access points.\n• Mark secondary access points with reflective markers so responders can identify alternate routes onto the property."
